"Art forms that appeal to modern leftish intellectuals tend to focus on
sordidness, defeat and despair, or else they take on an orgiastic tone,
throwing off rational control as if there were no hope of accomplishing
anything through rational calculation and all that was left was to immerse
oneself in the sensations of the moment."  (ISAIF, para. 17)







